    {
      "commentary": {
        "commtxt": "England too came into this series with a bit of chaos. Ben Stokes had retired, Brendon McCullum had left, Stephen Fleming was named head coach but will only take over from the South Africa series, and Joe Root was reinstated as captain. They needed some steadying and calmness, and Root provided just that. England started with a thumping win at Headingley, although that was overshadowed by the Brydon Carse incident. Since then, they have put their heads down and focused on what matters most - performing on the field - and the result has been a 3-0 sweep.",
        "timestamp": 1789217697769,
        "overnum": 0.0,
        "inningsid": 4,
        "eventtype": "NONE",
        "commentaryformats": [
          {
            "type": "",
