    {
      "commentary": {
        "commtxt": "There are plenty of positives for England to carry into the new Fleming-Root regime in South Africa. Ollie Robinson was the standout with 21 wickets, combining accuracy with movement both ways and proving a handful on responsive pitches. The four-pronged pace attack complemented each other nicely throughout the series, while Jordan Cox and Daniel Lawrence made the most of their opportunities with the bat and will be pushing for an extended run in the XI. Root may not have scored a hundred this summer, but he remains England's best batter and will be expected to bounce back when they return to Test cricket in South Africa.",
        "timestamp": 1789217682880,
        "overnum": 0.0,
