    {
      "commentary": {
        "commtxt": "This Test was Pakistan in a nutshell - mercurial, entertaining, sloppy and inconsistent. There were moments, particularly from Razaullah, that made everyone sit up and go wow, and there were others when it felt like the same old Pakistan. Before the Test, Mike Hesson was asked by Nasser Hussain whether the end would justify the means if Pakistan pulled off a win after all the upheaval. “Look, I can't really coin on that because, you know, I've been dealt a set of cards, and I have to make the most of it.” They did make the most of those cards. The first-innings batting did little to suggest that, but they fought hard with the ball and showed far greater application with the bat in the second essay. They came into the final day with a glimmer of hope and, had they taken the chances offered by Joe Root, who knows how the chase might have unfolded.",
        "timestamp": 1789217664680,
        "overnum": 0.0,
        "inningsid": 4,
        "eventtype": "NONE",
        "commentaryformats": [
