    {
      "commentary": {
        "commtxt": "They may have been whitewashed, but the radical changes made before this Test have at least produced some positives. They have unearthed a raw, unpolished gem in Razaullah, the biggest takeaway from this game. He bowled with pace and aggression, and then kept everyone on the edge of their seats with the bat. Azan Awais showed he can handle himself in this format and in these conditions with a gritty knock, while the old hands, Masood and Abbas, suggested they still have a few years left in them. There is something to build on here, but much will depend on how Pakistan handle these players from here.",
        "timestamp": 1789217659074,
        "overnum": 0.0,
        "inningsid": 4,
