    {
      "commentary": {
        "commtxt": "B0$ [On Jordan Cox's performance] Yeah, five dismissals have sort of gone under the radar, how well he did to step up and do the role that he did was outstanding, and to back that up with a brilliant knock today, showed great maturity, great calmness out there as well in that situation, and not having a huge amount of experience batting at number three, has taken to the role wonderfully. So really pleased for him, and hopefully takes a lot of confidence from it. [On what has pleased him most in this series] Actually just the amount of uncertainty about noise, and I guess chaos coming into the series, the way that the guys have dealt with that and been so clinical in what we've had thrown in front of us, and to come and be stood here 3-0 I think is really pleasing, and sets us up nicely for the start of a new era with Stephen Fleming coming in. But I don't think we would have been able to play in the manner that we have without the work that Brendon (McCullum) did as coach and Ben (Stokes) as captain. And I think it's a continuation and a small evolution of all the stuff that happened before this. So that has to continue forward, and we'll continue to keep trying to evolve that and improve on what's been a really good summer here. [On Marcus Trescothick's role as stand-in coach] I think he's been awesome. It can't be an easy thing when you know that it's not a long-term role, and for him to be able to sort of juggle between trying to look forward and what that might look like, but also be able to have his influence and his way of seeing the game on this group has been fantastic. I think he's got the balance brilliantly, and he'll be so much better for the experience, I'm sure too. But he's a wonderful coach, he's got a huge amount of respect from the group, and hopefully we get to work with him for a lot longer.",
        "timestamp": 1789217576818,
        "overnum": 0.0,
        "inningsid": 4,
        "eventtype": "NONE",
        "commentaryformats": [
