    },
    {
      "commentary": {
        "commtxt": "B0$ [On returning to the captaincy role and the 3-0 series win] We've had things go our own way a little bit throughout the series, and we had a little bit of pushback yesterday, which was, in a strange way, quite a good thing for the group. But for us to come through it and be so convincing in the way that we've finished the series off, and throughout the whole three games really, has been really pleasing. [You didn't know much about Razaullah, the batter?] No, we didn't. We didn't have a lot to work with, and fair play. He played some wonderful shots, made it quite difficult to set fields to, and struck the ball nicely. I don't know how he's not pulled a side really, he's swinging that hard. But fair play, he played nicely and made it difficult for us. At the start of the game, when you looked at that pitch, if you said you were chasing 130, you'd have taken it. And for us to get clinical towards the back end there, a big partnership to see us home, was exactly the sort of thing we're after, off the back of two other brilliant performances. So yeah, in many ways, out of this series there's a lot of information to work with, and puts us in a nice place going into the winter.",
        "timestamp": 1789217528538,
